clear_zbuff() clears twice what set_zbuff() allocated on LP64.

zbuff is an int array and set_zbuff sizes it with sizeof(int), but the clear
uses sizeof(long). Those matched on the 32-bit machines BB was written for;
on x86_64 the memset runs off the end of the allocation and corrupts the
heap, and the demo dies partway through with

    malloc(): corrupted top size

--- a/tex.c
+++ b/tex.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 
 static inline void clear_zbuff()
 {
-    memset(zbuff, 0x55, (X_s * Y_s * sizeof(long)));
+    memset(zbuff, 0x55, (X_s * Y_s * sizeof(int)));
 }
 
 
